Build 158r690 - 2026-06-30

- Consolidated the SQL backend into the main Perl tree by removing duplicated local SQL modules where appropriate.
- Integrated DME, DME Reference and EADB SQL support into the standard Perl modules.
- Consolidated SQL support for both MariaDB and SQLite backends.
- Introduced the new SQL table "badip" to replace the previous "badips" implementation, avoiding conflicts with existing installations while preserving backward compatibility.
- Added automatic creation and schema verification of the "badip" table for both MariaDB and SQLite backends.
- Updated all SQL code paths related to bad IP management to use the new "badip" table and its new schema.
- Preserved the legacy "badips" table unchanged for compatibility with previous SQL installations.
- Fixed an exception in DXChannel::check_cnum_debugging() when connection number debugging was enabled before the connection object was fully initialized.
- Fixed show/registered for SQL backends.
- Added the new show/regpass command to display registration and password status for one or all users.
- Updated SQL export/import utilities and SQL table reporting commands.
- Improved SQL startup consistency and automatic SQL object initialization.
- Updated the SQL upgrade documentation in both English and Spanish.
- General code cleanup, SQL consolidation and synchronization with the Docker/container build tree.
